In `accessibility.spec.ts`, create a test that navigates to a primary page (e.g., '/pi-controller'). Use the `AxeBuilder` to inject the axe-core script and analyze the page. The test should fail if any accessibility violations are found.

Pseudo-code:
```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
import AxeBuilder from '@axe-core/playwright';

test('should not have any automatically detectable accessibility issues', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/pi-controller');
  const accessibilityScanResults = await new AxeBuilder({ page })
    .withTags(['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa', 'wcag21a', 'wcag21aa'])
    .analyze();
  expect(accessibilityScanResults.violations).toEqual([]);
});
```
